  "review": [
    {
      "section": "time.clock",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "note": "'elekere {h}' + additive 'na nkeji N' (and N minutes) with Igbo numerals (ise, iri, iri na ise, iri abụọ ...), 'na ọkara' for half past. Chose additive for 35-55 over the subtractive 'ọ fọrọ nkeji iri ka ọ kụọ elekere atọ', which is longer and whose exact wording I am less sure of. Also changed noon 'ehihie' (afternoon/daytime) to 'etiti ehihie' (midday)."
    }
  ]
